727 0 obj
<<
/Title (The DNS \(Domain Name System\) translates domain names into IP addresses, enabling not just IoT devices but other clients, like web browsers, email clients, servers, data centers as well to communicate with cloud services. However, conventional DNS does not inherently authenticate such responses, making the users vulnerable to DNS spoofing and response manipulation. Here is where DNSSEC \(Domain Name System Security Extensions\) comes into play, which addresses these issues by using digital signatures and a chain of trust to authenticate DNS data and detect invalid responses.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 400 0 R
/Next 979 0 R
>>
endobj
